-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/79914580-9bcf-564a-8dac-61f5793b392f
-- title:
--   Supersingular prolongation: charts, node annuli, level orbits, Drinfeld quotient
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. Write $F_0 :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` for the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of the full modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\bar F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of the level structure given by `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$). The hypotheses are: a finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ (that field being the $\kappa$-subfield of Laurent series generated by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) together with `hW`, which says that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`; the inclusion `hle` $: F_0\le\bar F$; a constant reduction $R_0 :=$ `ConstantReduction A F_0 (modularFunctionFieldC κ M')`, that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F_0$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ (an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ iff it lies in $A$, and residues of constants are the $A$-residues), with the scaling property `exists_smul_mem` and a place map preserving degrees and compatible with pushforward of divisors; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $F_0$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and finally a chosen element $s\in W$, a supersingular place. Throughout, $\bar j$ denotes the image in $F_0$ of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ under `coeffEmb`, and places, their order functions $P.\mathrm{ord}$, their evaluation maps $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ and rationality are those of the project's `Place` structure.
--
--   The assertion is the existence of a type $F_{ss}$, a field structure on it, a $\kappa$-algebra structure, and a regular prolongation $R :=$ `RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') FSS` — a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, such that a constant lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ iff it lies in $A$, residues of constants are their $A$-residues, and every nonzero element of $\bar F$ can be scaled by a constant into $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue — such that the following hold.
--
--   First, $F_{ss}$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$. Second, $R$ specialises $R_0$ at $s$: for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of $F_0$ at which $\bar j$ has nonnegative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is the image in $F_{ss}$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$. Third, $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is invariant under the level automorphisms: for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, the pullback of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` equals $R.\mathrm{integers}$; here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $\bar F$ characterised by `IsLevelAutBar`, its prescribed effect on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ twisted by `conjElem q γ` under embeddings sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ (and the identity if no such automorphism exists).
--
--   Next, there exist a finset $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$, a family $Q\mapsto S_Q$ of subrings of $\bar F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q\colon A[X]\to S_Q$, ring homomorphisms $\chi_{0,Q}\colon S_Q\to\kappa$, and sets $D_Q$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the following properties.
--
--   (a) $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   (b) For every place $Q\notin N$, thirteen clauses hold: $S_Q$ contains the images of all elements of $A$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $\bar F$ for every $a\in A$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the $A$-residue of $a$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X))=0$; for every $c\in A$ with zero residue there is exactly one ring homomorphism $\chi\colon S_Q\to A$ with $\chi(\varphi_Q(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A$, with $A$-residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ for all $f\in S_Q$, and with $\chi(\varphi_Q(X))=c$; every $f\in S_Q$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue of that element in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ of $\bar F$ such that every $f\in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and such that for every $f\in S_Q$ the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_{0,Q}(f)=0$; every ring homomorphism $\chi\colon S_Q\to A$ which is the identity on the constants $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ and reduces to $\chi_{0,Q}$ is realised by a unique $P\in D_Q$, in the sense that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)=\chi(f)$ for all $f\in S_Q$; for every $P\in D_Q$, an element $f\in\bar F$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ iff $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_Q$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h)\neq0$; every nonzero $f\in\bar F$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}(f)=0$ for all $P\in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant $c\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and every $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $P\in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   (c) The discs are pairwise disjoint off $N$: if $Q,Q'\notin N$ and some place $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q=Q'$.
--
--   (d) No place of a disc is a cusp in the $j$-sense: for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_Q$, the $P$-order of the image of $\bar j$ in $\bar F$ is $\ge 0$.
--
--   (e) Level equivariance of $N$ and of the discs: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms of $\bar F$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and for any witness that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residue automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ satisfies: a place $Q$ lies in $N$ iff $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q$ does, and for $Q\notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ (Dx Q)` $=D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q}$, where `smulDisc τ D` is $\{P\mid \tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D\}$.
--
--   (f) Drinfeld identification of the reduced field: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every hypothesis that the coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $F_{ss}$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the subfield of the Drinfeld function field (the fraction field of `CoordRing q κ`) fixed by the automorphisms `hFunctionFieldAction q κ ⟨(1, ζ), _⟩` for $\zeta\in C_s$, such that the cardinality of $C_s$ equals $2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, that is, twice `jWidthChar q` of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; and such that $e$ intertwines the level action with the Drinfeld one: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every witness that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every witness that the pair (reduction of $\gamma$ modulo $q$, $1$) lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) — the kernel of the character $(g,u)\mapsto\det(g)\,u^{q+1}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)\times\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ — one has, for all $x\in F_{ss}$, that $e$ applied to $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1})\,x$, viewed in the Drinfeld function field, equals `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` of that pair applied to $e(x)$.
--
--   (g) Transport under semilinear automorphisms: let $g$ be an element of `SemilinearAut (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')`, i.e. a pair consisting of a ring automorphism of $\bar F$ and one of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible over the structure map, and assume: `hgA`, that the base automorphism of $g$ preserves $A$; `hgR`, that $g$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$; `hgj`, that $g$ fixes the image of $\bar j$ in $\bar F$; a ring automorphism $\psi$ of $\kappa$ with `hψ`, that $\psi$ of the $A$-residue of $a$ is the $A$-residue of the image of $a$ under the base automorphism; and a ring automorphism $\varphi$ of $F_{ss}$ with `hφ`, that the $R$-residue of $g\cdot f$ is $\varphi$ of the $R$-residue of $f$ for all $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$. Then for all places $Q,Q'$ of $F_{ss}$ with $Q\notin N$ and $Q'$ the transport of $Q$ along $\varphi$ (an element $y$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q'$ iff $\varphi^{-1}(y)$ lies in that of $Q$), one has $Q'\notin N$, and there is a witness that $f\in S_Q$ iff $g\cdot f\in S_{Q'}$, such that $\chi_{0,Q'}(g\cdot f)=\psi(\chi_{0,Q}(f))$ for $f\in S_Q$, and $P\in D_Q$ iff $g\cdot P\in D_{Q'}$ for every place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   (h) The level group acts transitively on $N$: for all $x,x'\in N$ there are $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a witness that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of that automorphism carrying $x$ to $x'$.
--
--   (i) No place off $N$ is fixed by the whole level group: for every $Q\notin N$ there are $\zeta$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a witness of invariance of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` moves $Q$.
--
--   (j) Generators of the affine ring: there exist $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and $g_0,\dots,g_{n-1}\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ such that each $g_i$ lies in the valuation subring of every $P\in D_Q$ with $Q\notin N$ and has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(g_i)\in A$ there, and such that every $f\in F_{ss}$ lying in the valuation subring of every place $Q\notin N$ belongs to the $\kappa$-subalgebra of $F_{ss}$ generated by the $R$-residues of the $g_i$.
--
--   (k) Annuli at the places of $N$: there exists a map $x\mapsto An(x)$ from places of $F_{ss}$ to annuli `Annulus A (fieldBar q M')` — each given by a domain of places of $\bar F$, a parameter, and a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the structure's axioms: each place of the domain is rational, the parameter lies in its valuation subring with value in the maximal ideal of $A$ and nonzero, the modulus factors as that value times an element of the maximal ideal, each admissible value is attained by exactly one place of the domain, the order of the parameter minus its value is $1$, and the unit principle — such that: for each $x\in N$, the parameter of $An(x)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $x$-order $1$, and for every $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue and with $P.\mathrm{ord}(f)=0$ for all $P$ in the domain of $An(x)$, at each such $P$ the element $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\cdot P.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{param})^{-x.\mathrm{ord}(R.\mathrm{residue}\,f)}$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there; the modulus of $An(x)$ is nonzero in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; no place of the domain of $An(x)$ lies in any $D_Q$ with $Q\notin N$; and every place $P$ in the domain of $An(x)$ specialises to $s$, in the sense that for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is nonnegative at every place where $\bar j$ has nonnegative order and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose $A$-residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ minus $a$ lies in $A$ and in its maximal ideal. Moreover the annuli attached to distinct elements of $N$ have disjoint domains; for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every $x\in N$, `smulDisc τ` of the domain of $An(x)$ is the domain of $An(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot x)$; and finally the charts and annuli cover: every rational place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which satisfies the same specialisation-to-$s$ condition just described lies either in $D_Q$ for some $Q\notin N$, or in the domain of $An(x)$ for some $x\in N$.
--
--   This is the supersingular local model for the full level-$q$ modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with level structure the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: a single regular prolongation of $A$ whose reduced field is a quotient of the Drinfeld curve $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-curve, equipped with smooth-point charts off a set of $q+1$ node places, annuli at those node places, the level-group orbit structure on them, and a finite set of generators of the affine ring of the reduced curve. It is the form of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_inertia`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_inertia) in which the auxiliary data of a $(q^2-1)$-st root of $q$ inside $A$ no longer appears among the hypotheses, and it feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algEquiv_quotField_of_chart_over`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algEquiv_quotField_of_chart_over), which extracts the identification of the reduced field with a Drinfeld quotient field at a chart.
